From 1dda0e342994d6eb93da526feeb44d3f2cc9bc4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruilin Gao <ruiling@andrew.cmu.edu>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:35:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [rollout] feat: explicit Continuous Token model_family
 override with an actionable construction error

DeepSeek-R1 distills keep Qwen model_type values (qwen2/qwen3) but ship
DeepSeek's tokenizer and chat template, in which <|im_end|> is renamed
away. Since #6804 the builder family is an exact model_type lookup, so
QwenContinuousTokenBuilder.__init__ raises "Tokenizer does not define
required token '<|im_end|>'" before any rollout starts (#7637), and no
config can route around it: #6804 removed data.continuous_token.

Restore data.continuous_token.model_family (the override only, not the
removed enable toggle): auto keeps the exact model_type inference, an
explicit family selects the builder matching the checkpoint's chat
template. When the auto-inferred builder cannot be constructed because a
required token is missing, the error now names the override and the
family these checkpoints need, instead of only naming the missing token.
An explicitly requested family that cannot construct still raises the
original error, and require_token_id raises MissingRequiredTokenError (a
ValueError subclass) for the token-absent case so the factory rewraps
exactly that.
